458b02ccfda22411f844074a.text:
{
  "headline": "Boca Raton to Host 2nd Annual Mobility Workshop on Thursday, October 29, 2026",
  "dek": "Residents can learn about current transportation projects and view student innovations at Florida Atlantic University.",
  "body_md": "The City of Boca Raton will host its 2nd Annual Mobility Workshop on Thursday, October 29, 2026, from 4:30 to 7:00 pm at Florida Atlantic University (FAU).\n\nThe free event will take place in Gangal Hall at FAU’s Engineering East building. It is presented in partnership with the FAU College of Engineering & Computer Science and the FAU Chapter of the Institute of Transportation Engineers. Pre-registration is required due to limited capacity.\n\nAttendees can connect with local transportation agencies and partners during an exhibit hall from 4:30 to 5:30 p.m. Participating organizations include the Palm Beach Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO), Florida Department of Transportation (FDOT), Circuit, the City of Boca Raton’s Fire Rescue Services Department, and the Office of Sustainability.\n\nFrom 5:30 to 6:00 p.m., the City’s Public Works & Engineering staff will provide updates on current mobility programs. The event will conclude with student poster presentations from 6:00 to 7:00 p.m., featuring ideas from FAU students for the future of mobility.\n\nResidents can visit the City’s Mobility Workshop webpage for more information and to register.",
  "beat": "government",
  "source_record_ids": [
    "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The City of Boca Raton will host its 2nd Annual Mobility Workshop on Thursday, October 29, 2026, from 4:30 to 7:00 pm at Florida Atlantic University (FAU).",
      "record_id": "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
    },
    {
      "text": "The free event will take place in Gangal Hall at FAU’s Engineering East building.",
      "record_id": "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is presented in partnership with the FAU College of Engineering & Computer Science and the FAU Chapter of the Institute of Transportation Engineers.",
      "record_id": "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-registration is required due to limited capacity.",
      "record_id": "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
    },
    {
      "text": "Participating organizations include the Palm Beach Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO), Florida Department of Transportation (FDOT), Circuit, the City of Boca Raton’s Fire Rescue Services Department, and the Office of Sustainability.",
      "record_id": "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
    },
    {
      "text": "The City’s Public Works & Engineering staff will provide updates on current mobility programs from 5:30 to 6:00 p.m.",
      "record_id": "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
    },
    {
      "text": "FAU students will share innovative ideas for the future of mobility during student poster presentations from 6:00 to 7:00 p.m.",
      "record_id": "dc5febf4-5aea-42d5-855f-eff3361b2264"
    }
  ]
}

