d508f203f34568da64fbfed5.text:
{
  "headline": "Boca Raton Night Market Returns to Sanborn Square",
  "dek": "The monthly evening event features food, local art, music, and free shuttle service starting in October.",
  "body_md": "The City of Boca Raton's Night Market series returns to Sanborn Square, located at 72 N Federal Hwy, starting Thursday, Oct. 1, 2026. The evening event runs from 6–9 p.m.\n\nThe seasonal market will take place monthly on Oct. 1, Nov. 5, and Dec. 10, 2026. The December event will feature a holiday theme.\n\nEach Night Market transforms Sanborn Square into an open-air festival. Vendors offer traditional market fare like baked goods and sweet treats, alongside local artists and makers. Music will fill the air throughout the evening.\n\nAttendees can take advantage of free rides to and from the Night Market with BocaConnect, the City's eco-friendly shuttle service. Residents can download the Circuit App to request a ride in just a few clicks.\n\n\"Our Night Markets are one of the best ways to experience everything that makes Boca Raton special — great food, local art, music, and a real sense of community,\" said Mayor Andy Thomson.",
  "beat": "community",
  "source_record_ids": [
    "ab7018ab-9a75-49b5-8943-abb9fb042419"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
