{
  "headline": "Boca Raton Launches October Halloween Events and Howl-O-Ween",
  "dek": "The city's Recreation Services Department is rolling out month-long family and pet-friendly Halloween programming.",
  "body_md": "Boca Raton is celebrating the Halloween season with a lineup of events for residents and their pets throughout October 2026. The City’s Recreation Services Department is presenting Boo-ca Boo Days, offering month-long programming at local parks, libraries, and community centers.\n\nThe canine celebration Howl-O-Ween will take place on Saturday, Oct. 24, 2026, from 9 a.m. to 12 p.m. at Countess de Hoernle Park. The free event features a morning of costumes, contests, and activities for dogs and their owners.\n\nThe Howl-O-Ween schedule includes the Muttville Comix Dog Show at 9:30 a.m., the Howl-O-Weener Dog Race Contest at 10:30 a.m., and the Howl-O-Ween Costume Contest at 11:30 a.m. Attendees can also enjoy a Trail of Treats, photo booth, paw spa, crafts, and hydration stations. All dogs must remain on a leash, and owners are required to clean up after their pets.\n\nAlongside the pet-centric morning, Boo-ca Boo Days provides a variety of activities across the city. Highlights include the Silly Spooky Bubble Party on Saturday, Oct. 3, at the Boca Raton Public Library's Spanish River location; Ghostly Glows and Ghoulish Gases at the Children’s Science Explorium on Oct. 17 and 18; and a Family Halloween Feature Film screening of Hocus Pocus (1993) on Friday, Oct. 30, also at the Spanish River library patio.\n\nBoca Raton was recognized as a certified Better Cities for Pets™ city in 2024, highlighting its pet-friendly parks and programs, such as Mizner Bark Dog Park and Bark Beach at Spanish River Park.\n\nResidents can find full schedules, registration requirements, and event costs for Boo-ca Boo Days online at myboca.us/2813/Boca-Boo-Days-Events, and information for Howl-O-Ween at myboca.us/3016/Howl-O-Ween.",
  "beat": "community",
  "source_record_ids": [
    "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The City’s Recreation Services Department is presenting Boo-ca Boo Days, offering month-long programming at local parks, libraries, and community centers.",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "The canine celebration Howl-O-Ween will take place on Saturday, Oct. 24, 2026, from 9 a.m. to 12 p.m. at Countess de Hoernle Park.",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "The free event features a morning of costumes, contests, and activities for dogs and their owners.",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Howl-O-Ween schedule includes the Muttville Comix Dog Show at 9:30 a.m., the Howl-O-Weener Dog Race Contest at 10:30 a.m., and the Howl-O-Ween Costume Contest at 11:30 a.m.",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "Attendees can also enjoy a Trail of Treats, photo booth, paw spa, crafts, and hydration stations.",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "All dogs must remain on a leash, and owners are required to clean up after their pets.",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "Highlights include the Silly Spooky Bubble Party on Saturday, Oct. 3, at the Boca Raton Public Library's Spanish River location",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ghostly Glows and Ghoulish Gases at the Children’s Science Explorium on Oct. 17 and 18",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
    },
    {
      "text": "Family Halloween Feature Film screening of Hocus Pocus (1993) on Friday, Oct. 30, also at the Spanish River library patio.",
      "record_id": "9e7fd7c2-a5a2-4ea0-80bd-11972f95b23a"
