{
  "headline": "City to Host Red, White & Boca Veterans Day Celebration",
  "dek": "The free event at Mizner Park Amphitheater will feature live music, a classic car show, and a Veterans Marketplace on Nov. 11.",
  "body_md": "The City of Boca Raton will host Red, White & Boca: A Veterans Day Celebration on Wednesday, November 11, 2026, from 4:00 to 7:00 p.m. at the Mizner Park Amphitheater, located at 590 Plaza Real.\n\nThe free event is open to veterans, their families, and community members of all ages with no registration required. The afternoon will feature live music, speeches, a Veterans Marketplace showcasing local service organizations and veteran-owned small businesses, and food vendors.\n\nPerformances are scheduled from The Coastman Chorus and Belladiva. The event's east lawn will host a classic car show, featuring award presentations at 6:45 p.m. for categories including Best of Show and Best Veteran-Owned.\n\nThe event begins at 4:00 p.m., followed by the Presentation of Colors and National Anthem at 4:45 p.m. Speeches are slated for 4:55 p.m. and 5:25 p.m., with The Coastman Chorus performing at 5:10 p.m. Announcements will take place at 5:40 p.m., and Belladiva will perform at 5:45 p.m.\n\nBoca Raton is recognized as a Purple Heart City, honoring military veterans who have received the Purple Heart for bravery and valor in the line of duty. More information and online marketplace applications are available at myboca.us/1467/Veterans-Day.",
